; 13.4 - Proto-Chumash to Obispeño
; citation: CatDoom, from Klar, Kathryn (1977), Topics in Historical Chumash Grammar. <http://linguistics.berkeley.edu/~survey/documents/dissertations/klar-1977.pdf>
Sʼ / ʔ
q k / {q,k} {k(ʃ),tʲ} (allophonic)
{ˀm,ˀn} / {∅,ʔ} (the former is more likely)
ˀw / w (may have remained glottalized)
ˀj / ∅